.TH "kitten-command-palette" 1 "Jul 30, 2026" "0.48.2" "kitty"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
kitten-command-palette \- Browse and trigger keyboard shortcuts and actions
.SH "نمای کلی (OVERVIEW)"
.sp
The command palette lets you browse, search and trigger all keyboard shortcuts
and actions in \fIkitty\fP from a single searchable overlay. Press
\fBctrl+shift+f3\fP \%<#\:shortcut-kitty\:.Command-palette> to open it (default: \fBCtrl\fP+\fBShift\fP+\fBF3\fP).
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 2.5
The command palette showing search results for \fBwin close\fP\&. (images not supported)
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
All mapped actions (those with a keyboard shortcut) and unmapped actions (those
available but not bound to any key) are listed, organized by category. Mouse
bindings are shown in a separate section. Simply type to search, select a
result, and press \fBEnter\fP to run it.
.SH Searching
.sp
As you type into the search bar, the palette filters results in real time.
Matching is case\-insensitive and works across three columns simultaneously:
the \fBkey\fP (keyboard shortcut), the \fBaction\fP name, and the \fBcategory\fP\&.
Matched characters are highlighted so you can see exactly where each term hit.
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
\fBMultiple words\fP
Separate your terms with spaces. Typing \fBscroll page\fP looks for items
that contain \fIscroll\fP and \fIpage\fP anywhere across the key, action, or
category columns. Items that match more of your terms are ranked higher
than those that match fewer.
.TP
\fBHow individual words are matched\fP
Each word in your query is compared against every word in the three
columns. The best match wins and determines the item\(aqs score for that
term:
.INDENT 7.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fIExact word\fP — the query word equals a column word exactly (highest score).
.IP \(bu 2
\fIPrefix\fP — the column word starts with the query word,
e.g. \fBscr\fP matches \fBscroll\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
\fITypo tolerance\fP — for words of four characters or longer, a single
typo (one character inserted, deleted, or substituted) still produces a
match, and two typos give a lower\-scoring match.
.UNINDENT
.sp
An item appears in the results as long as at least one query word matches
something. Items where more query words match rank above those where fewer
match.
.TP
\fBCompound names\fP
Delimiters such as \fB_\fP, \fB+\fP, \fB/\fP, and \fB\-\fP are kept intact inside a
query word, so you can search for compound action names as a unit.
Typing \fBmouse_selection\fP first tries to find that exact substring in each
column. If that fails, it splits the token into its parts (\fBmouse\fP and
\fBselection\fP) and matches each part independently against the column words.
.TP
\fBRanking\fP
When multiple items match the same query, they are sorted by:
.INDENT 7.0
.IP 1. 3
Number of query words that matched (more is better).
.IP 2. 3
Score on the action column (action matches outrank key or category matches).
.IP 3. 3
Score on the key column.
.IP 4. 3
Score on the category column.
.IP 5. 3
Shorter action name as a tiebreaker (more specific results first).
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH Keyboard controls
.sp
The following keys are available while the command palette is open:
.TS
box center;
l|l.
T{
Key
T}	T{
Action
T}
_
T{
Any text
T}	T{
Filter results by typing a search query
T}
_
T{
\fBEnter\fP
T}	T{
Run the selected action
T}
_
T{
\fBEscape\fP
T}	T{
Clear the search query, or close the palette if the query is already empty
T}
_
T{
\fBUp\fP / \fBCtrl\fP+\fBK\fP / \fBCtrl\fP+\fBP\fP
T}	T{
Move selection up
T}
_
T{
\fBDown\fP / \fBCtrl\fP+\fBJ\fP / \fBCtrl\fP+\fBN\fP
T}	T{
Move selection down
T}
_
T{
\fBPage Up\fP
T}	T{
Move selection up by a page
T}
_
T{
\fBPage Down\fP
T}	T{
Move selection down by a page
T}
_
T{
\fBHome\fP
T}	T{
Jump to the first result
T}
_
T{
\fBEnd\fP
T}	T{
Jump to the last result
T}
_
T{
\fBBackspace\fP
T}	T{
Delete the last character from the query
T}
_
T{
\fBF12\fP
T}	T{
Toggle display of unmapped actions
T}
_
T{
Mouse click
T}	T{
Select and run the clicked action
T}
.TE
.SH Unmapped actions
.sp
By default, the palette shows both mapped actions (those bound to a shortcut)
and unmapped actions (those with no shortcut assigned). Unmapped actions appear
with an \fB(unmapped)\fP label in the key column. Press \fBF12\fP to toggle
their visibility. This preference is remembered across sessions.
.sp
Unmapped actions are useful for discovering functionality that you may not have
configured a shortcut for. You can run them directly from the palette, or note
the action name and add a mapping in \fBkitty.conf\fP\&.
.SH Custom keyboard modes
.sp
If you have defined custom keyboard modes \%<#\:modal-mappings> in your
configuration, their bindings appear under separate mode headers in the palette.
The \fBpush_keyboard_mode\fP bindings are grouped with the target mode they
activate, making it easy to see how to enter each mode alongside its shortcuts.
.SH "پیکربندی (CONFIGURATION)"
.sp
The default mapping to open the command palette is:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
map kitty_mod+f3 command_palette
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
You can change this in \fBkitty.conf\fP like any other mapping. For example:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
map ctrl+p command_palette
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH "نویسنده (AUTHOR)"

